{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ee81dee8-c2b7-4fcd-ae5c-6ed9795ba137","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7fd3609935e2325","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-ir28dcb0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Link registered model versions to producing runs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: a registered model\nversion records a reference to the run (training or pipeline run) that produced\nit, so that downstream consumers — including the Dashboard's comparison\ncapability — can resolve which run created a given model version. The registry\nalready serves as the source of truth for training lineage; this epic extends\nthat lineage to the run level.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Recording, on registered model versions, a reference to the run that\n  produced them, using the Model Registry's existing extension point for\n  structured metadata on model versions (the mechanism is an implementation\n  decision for the Model Registry team).\n- Exposing the run reference through the Model Registry's existing REST\n  interface so that clients can retrieve the producing run for a model\n  version.\n- Support for both training-run and pipeline-run references.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered after this change, when it is created from\n  a run, then the version carries a reference to that producing run that is\n  retrievable via the Model Registry REST API.\n- Given a model version with a run reference, when the reference is resolved,\n  then it identifies the run within the same project (single-project scope per\n  the strategy's out-of-scope list).\n- Given model versions registered before this change, when queried, then they\n  remain readable with no regression (absence of a run reference on legacy\n  versions is handled gracefully).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them (registry-side linkage; the Dashboard-facing entry point that opens a\n  comparison from the registry is delivered separately by the Dashboard team).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29694,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe13c7a24194c50","agent_id":"af5460c6b6aede141","session_id":"247f599f-8d1b-4cae-a1c4-a0bcc18e8506","uuid":"18eb78d4-febb-4c3e-9af0-fd68bdc60754","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:13:17.755Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
