{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ee81dee8-c2b7-4fcd-ae5c-6ed9795ba137","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3e9997f50423db6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-ir28dcb0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E003.md","content":"# Open run comparison from the Model Registry view\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Model Registry entry point for run comparison: from a\nregistered model version in the Dashboard's registry view, users can open the\nrun comparison capability populated with the run that produced that version,\nwithout navigating back to the runs list. The Dashboard owns the registry UI,\nso this epic is owned by the Dashboard team and builds on two prerequisites:\nthe run comparison view (its navigation target) and the run linkage recorded on\nregistered model versions (its data source).\n\n## Scope\n\n- An action on a registered model version in the Dashboard's Model Registry\n  view that opens the run comparison view populated with the producing run.\n- Graceful handling of model versions that carry no run reference (legacy\n  versions registered before linkage existed).\n- Single-project scope: the opened comparison stays within the model version's\n  project.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a registered model version that carries a producing-run reference,\n  when the user activates the compare action in the registry view, then the\n  run comparison view opens with the producing run pre-selected.\n- Given a registered model version with no run reference, when the registry\n  view is displayed, then the compare affordance is absent or disabled without\n  errors.\n- Given the compare action is used, when the comparison view opens, then the\n  user can add further runs from the same project to the comparison.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: \"so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry\" —\n  the Dashboard-facing half of HLR-2, delivered by the Dashboard team which\n  owns the registry UI.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29694,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe13c7a24194c50","agent_id":"af5460c6b6aede141","session_id":"247f599f-8d1b-4cae-a1c4-a0bcc18e8506","uuid":"0836d673-1c9b-4712-bc4b-86b046f73e9e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:13:23.201Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
