[\"E004 Documentation\"]\n71\t    E002 --> E004\n72\t    E003[\"E003 Registry entry point (Dashboard)\"] --> E004\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\t## DAG Justification\n76\t\n77\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n78\t|------|------|-----------|\n79\t| E001 → E003 | 12 (framework → consumer) | The registry entry point navigates to the comparison view; it builds against the comparison surface E001 delivers and cannot be built or validated before that surface exists. |\n80\t| E002 → E003 | 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry entry point's code consumes the run-linkage data recorded on registered model versions; it builds against that data, so it is serialized after the linkage work. |\n81\t| E001 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n82\t| E002 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n83\t| E003 → E004 | 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n84\t\n85\tParallel non-edges:\n86\t\n87\t| Pair | Rule | Rationale |\n88\t|------|------|-----------|\n89\t| E001 ∥ E002 | 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Dashboard (odh-dashboard) and Model Registry (model-registry) are separate components and repos with no shared artifact between the comparison view and the run-linkage recording. They proceed in parallel. |\n90\t\n91\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n92\t\n93\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n94\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n95\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Select 2+ runs, side-by-side parameters and metrics in the Dashboard. |\n96\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 | **Consolidated with HLR-1, not split**: the \"diff\" view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data (same component, same team — the strategy itself notes requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording). Splitting would produce two epics building the same surface plus an artificial serialization edge; covered by the single comparison epic at the higher priority (P0). |\n97\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002, E003 | Split